{"name":"Wild Strawberry","hex":"#ff3399","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wild strawberry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the species of strawberry that grows naturally throughout much of the Northern Hemisphere, Fragaria vesca.","Any of several species of plants resembling true strawberries, such as Indian strawberry (Potentilla indica, syn. Fragaria indica)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild_strawberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fragaria","blocks":[{"text":"Fragaria is a genus of flowering plants in the rose family, Rosaceae, commonly known as strawberries for their edible fruits. There are more than 20 described species and many hybrids and cultivars. The most common strawberries grown commercially are cultivars of the garden strawberry, a hybrid known as Fragaria × ananassa. Strawberries have a taste that varies by cultivar, and ranges from quite sweet to rather tart. Strawberries are an important commercial fruit crop, widely grown in all temperate regions of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/103_Fragaria_vesca_L.jpg/330px-103_Fragaria_vesca_L.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fragaria","wikidata":"Q745"},{"title":"Fragaria vesca","blocks":[{"text":"Fragaria vesca, commonly called the woodland strawberry, Alpine strawberry, wild strawberry, Carpathian strawberry or European strawberry, is a perennial herbaceous plant in the rose family that grows naturally throughout much of the Northern Hemisphere, and that produces edible fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Illustration_Fragaria_vesca0.jpg/330px-Illustration_Fragaria_vesca0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fragaria_vesca","wikidata":"Q146684"},{"title":"Wild Strawberry (manga)","blocks":[{"text":"Wild Strawberry  is a Japanese manga series written and illustrated by Ire Yonemoto. It was serialized on Shueisha's Shōnen Jump+ manga service from July 2023 to August 2025."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/Wild_Strawberry_volume_1_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Strawberry_(manga)","wikidata":"Q125125008"},{"title":"Strawberry","blocks":[{"text":"The garden strawberry is a widely grown hybrid plant cultivated worldwide for its fruit. The genus Fragaria, the strawberries, is in the rose family, Rosaceae. The fruit is appreciated for its aroma, bright red colour, juicy texture, and sweetness. It is eaten either fresh or in prepared foods such as jam, ice cream, and chocolates. Artificial strawberry flavourings and aromas are widely used in commercial products. Botanically, the strawberry is not a berry, but an aggregate accessory fruit. Each apparent 'seed' on the outside of the strawberry is actually an achene, a botanical fruit with a seed inside it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg/330px-Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry","wikidata":"Q13158"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Fragaria_daltoniana.jpg/330px-Fragaria_daltoniana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Fragaria_daltoniana.jpg/330px-Fragaria_daltoniana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fragaria daltoniana, a species from the Himalayas","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFragaria_daltoniana.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/